{"id":137,"flavor":[{"games":["Legends: Arceus"],"text":"It has no discernible heartbeat and does not seem to draw breath, and yet it appears to function without issue. I cannot even begin to explain this utterly bizarre anomaly."},{"games":["Shield"],"text":"In recent years, this species has been very helpful in cyberspace. These Pokémon will go around checking to make sure no suspicious data exists."},{"games":["Sword"],"text":"State-of-the-art technology was used to create Porygon. It was the first artificial Pokémon to be created via computer programming."},{"games":["Let’s Go, Eevee!","Let’s Go, Pikachu!"],"text":"The only Pokémon that people anticipate can fly into space. None has managed the feat yet, however."},{"games":["Ultra Moon"],"text":"It was built 20 years ago by scientists who dreamed of exploring space. Their dreams have yet to come true."},{"games":["Ultra Sun"],"text":"This Pokémon was created using the cutting-edge science of 20 years ago, so many parts of it have since become obsolete."},{"games":["Moon"],"text":"It can convert its body into digital data, which enables it to enter cyberspace."},{"games":["Sun"],"text":"Roughly 20 years ago, it was artificially created, utilizing the latest technology of the time."},{"games":["Alpha Sapphire","Omega Ruby","Sapphire","Ruby"],"text":"Porygon is capable of reverting itself entirely back to program data and entering cyberspace. This Pokémon is copy protected so it cannot be duplicated by copying."},{"games":["Y","LeafGreen"],"text":"A Pokémon that consists entirely of programming code. It is capable of moving freely in cyberspace."},{"games":["X","SoulSilver","Silver"],"text":"A man-made Pokémon that came about as a result of research. It is programmed with only basic motions."},{"games":["White 2","Black 2","White","Black","Platinum"],"text":"A man-made Pokémon created using advanced scientific means. It can move freely in cyberspace."},{"games":["HeartGold","Gold"],"text":"It is a manmade Pokémon. Since it doesn’t breathe, people are eager to try it in any environment."},{"games":["Pearl","Diamond"],"text":"The world’s first artificially created Pokémon. It can travel through electronic space."}],"abilities":[{"name":"Trace","hidden":false,"description":"When it enters a battle, the Pokémon copies an opposing Pokémon's Ability."},{"name":"Download","hidden":false,"description":"The Pokémon compares an opposing Pokémon's Defense and Sp. Def stats before raising its own Attack or Sp. Atk stat—whichever will be more effective."},{"name":"Analytic","hidden":true,"description":"Boosts the power of the Pokémon's move if it is the last to act that turn."}],"eggGroups":["Mineral"],"genderRate":-1,"hatchCounter":20,"baseHappiness":70,"growthRate":"medium","habitat":"urban","color":"Pink","shape":"Legs","evolution":{"id":137,"name":"Porygon","condition":null,"children":[{"id":233,"name":"Porygon2","condition":"Trade, holding Upgrade","children":[{"id":474,"name":"Porygon-Z","condition":"Trade, holding Dubious Disc","children":[]}]}]},"moves":{"game":"Scarlet / Violet","level":[[1,33],[1,160],[5,278],[10,393],[15,84],[20,60],[25,176],[30,97],[35,105],[40,435],[45,161],[50,38],[55,199],[60,192]],"machine":[97,59,268,451,38,598,527,203,263,492,416,356,63,58,196,182,60,94,473,240,156,247,214,76,164,241,129,36,851,168,87,86,85,271,433,428],"egg":[],"tutor":[]},"cards":[{"id":"sv10-153","name":"Team Rocket's Porygon","set":"Destined Rivals","date":"2025-05-30","rarity":"Common","number":"153","artist":null,"img":"sv10/153"},{"id":"sv4-142","name":"Porygon","set":"Paradox Rift","date":"2023-11-03","rarity":"Common","number":"142","artist":"Taiga Kayama","img":"sv4/142"},{"id":"sv3pt5-137","name":"Porygon","set":"151","date":"2023-09-22","rarity":"Common","number":"137","artist":"5ban Graphics","img":"sv3pt5/137"},{"id":"swsh11-140","name":"Porygon","set":"Lost Origin","date":"2022-09-09","rarity":"Common","number":"140","artist":"kurumitsu","img":"swsh11/140"},{"id":"swsh6-1